 ## Queue and Tickets
 
+### Queue
+
+A **queue** belongs to one entity and has:
+
+- `name`, `slug` (unique within the entity), `is_active` flag (default `true`) and optional `labels_i18n` (JSON, locale → label).
+- Issuance into an inactive queue is rejected with `App\Exceptions\InactiveQueueException`. The action re-reads the queue row inside the transaction (locked), so a queue deactivated after the caller loaded it is still rejected and nothing is persisted.
+
 ### Ticket
 
-Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `called_at` and `called_by` (filled when called). Attributes:
+Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call**. Attributes:
 
 - Source queue — the ticket belongs to **one** queue (within the entity); does not record which totem it came from.
-- Priority (numeric, see below).
-- Issuance timestamp (ordering "oldest first" within same priority).
-- Issuance channel: totem, virtual, printed copy, etc.
+- Display `code` — per-queue sequence `A001`, `A002`, … (prefix `A`, at least 3 zero-padded digits; grows past 999 as `A1000`, `A1001`, …), unique per `(queue_id, code)`. The next code is "last valid code + 1" by insertion order: deleting a ticket does not reuse its number (after `A001`..`A003` with `A002` deleted, the next is `A004`); malformed legacy codes (anything not matching `A<digits>`) are skipped (only `A-X` present → next is `A001`; `A001` then `A-X` → next is `A002`). Computed by `App\Models\Ticket::nextCode()`.
+- Priority (numeric, see below; integer `>= 0`, default `0`).
+- Issuance timestamp `issued_at` (ordering "oldest first" within same priority); new tickets get `issued_at = now()`.
+- Issuance channel: `totem`, `virtual` (default), `printed` (`App\Enums\TicketChannel`); there is no FK to totems.
+- Status: `waiting` (initial) or `called` (`App\Enums\TicketStatus`); there is no cancelled status.
+- Call fields `called_at` and `called_by_user_id` (nullable FK to users), filled exactly once when called.
+
+**Issuance** (`App\Actions\IssueTicket`, invokable, no constructor arguments: `__invoke(Queue $queue, int $priority = 0, TicketChannel $channel = TicketChannel::Virtual): Ticket`) runs in a transaction, rejects inactive queues and negative priorities (`InvalidArgumentException`), and retries a few times on a unique `(queue_id, code)` collision from concurrent issuance.
+
+**Write-once:** after issuance every ticket field is immutable except `status`, `called_at`, `called_by_user_id` (and `updated_at`). Any Eloquent save/update changing another field (e.g. `code`, `priority`) throws `LogicException`.
+
+**Single call** (`App\Models\Ticket::call(User $user): void`): marks the ticket `called` and records `called_at` plus the calling user. Only members of the ticket's entity may call (others get `Illuminate\Auth\Access\AuthorizationException`, ticket unchanged); calling a non-waiting ticket throws `LogicException`. Selection of *which* ticket to call next (priority/fairness) is not implemented yet — see below.
 
 ### Priority
 
